/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Two things about the math, displayed in the worksheet on page 13, are worth saying out loud. First, the example program in yellow isn't a horror story. 50% 90-day retention is unremarkable in an industry where annual attrition routinely exceeds 50%, and the improved scenario merely reaches the standard 75%+ benchmark.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (Second, notice what the recovery does not require: no headcount growth, no larger sourcing budget, no lower bar. It requires early quits to stop, which is a screening and process problem, not a spending problem. That's what makes this the rare seven-figure line item that can be recovered without a seven-figure investment. And a 25-point swing is not hypothetical: page 11 shows a program that did it while hiring volume hit an all-time high.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
